justification:"For gamma<1/2, agamma-beta0=2-3*gamma>0, and multiplying theta-gamma by the positive denominator 5/2-gamma gives gamma^2-gamma/2+1/2=(gamma-1/4)^2+7/16>0. At gamma=1/2 the numerator and denominator are 11/8 and 17/8, and 11/17>1/2. Above 1/2, beta0=gamma-1<=0=agamma and (1+gamma)/2-gamma=(1-gamma)/2>=0. The upper beta bounds and 0<=agamma<1 follow directly in each case. This note verifies arithmetic only, not epsilon admissibility."
