justification:"log(tau)<=0, so (theta-gamma)log(tau)<=0. Exponentiating gives tau^(theta-gamma)<=1; multiplying by tau^gamma>0 gives the claim. A common bound is an upper bound of the entire set of norm values, so the supremum has the same bound. No exchange of integrals or limits is involved."
