justification:"Dinv is bounded H^gamma to H^(1+gamma): on nonzero integers, <k>^2/|k|^2<=2. The Airy group preserves every Fourier Sobolev norm and is strongly continuous, by convergence on finitely many modes and uniformly small square-summable tails. For r=1+gamma>1/2, H^r is a multiplication algebra: weighted convolution is bounded in ell^2 using <k>^r<=C_r(<l>^r+<k-l>^r), the ell^1-ell^2 convolution inequality and ||hat h||_ell^1<= (sum <k>^(-2r))^(1/2)||h||_(H^r). The latter series converges for r>1/2. Thus the products in the endpoint formula depend continuously on time in H^r. Pnz is bounded, and the outer Airy group preserves this continuity. Subtracting the fixed initial endpoint gives a continuous stage. The inclusion H^r into H^agamma is bounded because agamma<=r. These facts justify representatives and the routine bounded extension, without resolving the separate epsilon hypothesis."
}
